. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/conf=
iguration/config-files.html#watch">watch</a></p><p>Also in this release: ha=
rdened workspace trust boundaries =E2=80=94 file tools can no longer reach =
outside the working directory through symbolic links, and project-local con=
fig only takes effect after the workspace is trusted; new <code>auto_sessio=
n_title</code> config to turn off automatic session title generation by cli=
ents. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/=
configuration/config-files.html#top-level-fields">Config files</a></p></div=
></div><div class=3D"wn-entry wn-hero"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=
=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code Desktop</span><h2 id=3D"kimi-code-desktop-is-here=
-september-17-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">Kimi Code=
 Desktop is here</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">September 17, 2026</span> <=
a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-co=
de/whats-new.html#kimi-code-desktop-is-here-september-17-2026" aria-label=
=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CKimi Code Desktop is here September 17, 2026=E2=
=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><p>The Kimi Code =
desktop client is officially available: it carries the Agent core of Kimi C=
ode CLI into a graphical interface, where you open a project, talk to the A=
gent, and ship changes in one window. Available now for macOS (Apple Silico=
n / Intel) and Windows. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs=
/en/kimi-code-desktop/getting-started.html">Quick Start</a></p><h4 id=3D"ev=
ery-step-stays-visible" tabindex=3D"-1">Every step stays visible <a class=
=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/what=
s-new.html#every-step-stays-visible" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CEv=
ery step stays visible=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Tool calls, thinking,=
 and the files changed in each turn are all presented in the interface; sen=
sitive operations raise approval prompts, and three permission modes (Alway=
s Ask / Ask When Needed / Never Ask) keep you in control. =E2=86=92 <a href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-desktop/task-execution-and-=
review.html#approvals-and-permissions">Handle approvals</a></p><h4 id=3D"a-=
complete-workflow-from-conversation-to-delivery" tabindex=3D"-1">A complete=
 workflow from conversation to delivery <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"=
https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#a-complete-workf=
low-from-conversation-to-delivery" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CA co=
mplete workflow from conversation to delivery=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><=
p>Goal mode keeps long-running objectives moving and can be paused, resumed=
, or cancelled; plan mode proposes an approach before touching files, and t=
he plan can be reviewed and refined; long tasks can move to the background,=
 where you can check progress or stop them at any time. =E2=86=92 <a href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-desktop/task-execution-and-=
review.html#task-modes">Choose a task mode</a></p><h4 id=3D"built-in-browse=
r-and-visual-annotation" tabindex=3D"-1">Built-in browser and visual annota=
tion <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/k=
imi-code/whats-new.html#built-in-browser-and-visual-annotation" aria-label=
=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CBuilt-in browser and visual annotation=E2=80=9D">=
=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The browser lives in the right panel, with tabs that s=
tay with the session and page context shared with the Agent; screenshot ann=
otation, text selection comments, <code>@</code> file mentions, and element=
 picking on web pages tell the Agent exactly what to change. =E2=86=92 <a h=
ref=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-desktop/task-execution-a=
nd-review.html#built-in-terminal">Verify in the terminal</a></p><p>Download=
: <a href=3D"https://code.kimi.com/kimi-code/desktop/download/KimiCode-mac-=
arm64.dmg" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">macOS =C2=B7 Apple Silicon<=
/a> =C2=B7 <a href=3D"https://code.kimi.com/kimi-code/desktop/download/Kimi=
Code-mac-x64.dmg" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">macOS =C2=B7 Intel</=
a> =C2=B7 <a href=3D"https://code.kimi.com/kimi-code/desktop/download/KimiC=
ode-win-x64.exe" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">Windows</a></p></div>=
</div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-prod=
uct">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v2-0-0-september-17-2026" tabindex=3D"-1=
