=3D"mermaid-diagrams-in-the-terminal" tabindex=3D"-1">Mermaid diagrams in t=
he terminal <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/do=
cs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#mermaid-diagrams-in-the-terminal" aria-label=
=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CMermaid diagrams in the terminal=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=
=8B</a></h4><p>Mermaid code blocks now render as diagrams in the terminal; =
turn this off under <code>/settings</code> =E2=86=92 Mermaid diagrams, or s=
et <code>mermaid =3D "off"</code> in the <code>[markdown]</code> section of=
 tui.toml.</p><p>Also in this release: the built-in browser plugin is renam=
ed to Kimi Browser Extension; when accumulated media in a session exceeds 2=
0 MB, the oldest images and videos are omitted from requests with a warning=
 =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/guide=
s/interaction.html#paste-images-and-videos">Paste images and videos</a>. Si=
nce v2.0.1, a provider's API key can be read from a named environment varia=
ble via <code>api_key_env</code> instead of being written into the config f=
ile =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/co=
nfiguration/config-files.html#providers">Config files</a>.</p></div></div><=
div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Ki=
mi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-43-0-september-14-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><spa=
n class=3D"ignore-header">v0.43.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">September =
14, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/cod=
e/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-43-0-september-14-2026" aria-label=3D=
"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.43.0 September 14, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></=
h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"ai-session-titles-in-web-on-by=
-default" tabindex=3D"-1">AI session titles in Web, on by default <a class=
=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/what=
s-new.html#ai-session-titles-in-web-on-by-default" aria-label=3D"Permalink =
to =E2=80=9CAI session titles in Web, on by default=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a>=
</h4><p>A title is generated automatically after the first turn, and you ca=
n regenerate it from the rename box =E2=80=94 no more naming sessions by ha=
nd.</p><h4 id=3D"delete-sessions-from-the-session-selector" tabindex=3D"-1"=
>Delete sessions from the session selector <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#delete-sessi=
ons-from-the-session-selector" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CDelete s=
essions from the session selector=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Select a s=
ession in the session selector, press <code>Ctrl-X</code>, then <code>y</co=
de> to confirm =E2=80=94 cleaning up old sessions is much easier.</p><h4 id=
=3D"fairer-time-budgets-in-goal-mode" tabindex=3D"-1">Fairer time budgets i=
n Goal Mode <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/do=
cs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#fairer-time-budgets-in-goal-mode" aria-label=
=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CFairer time budgets in Goal Mode=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=
=8B</a></h4><p>Time budgets no longer count the time while a session is clo=
sed, and the 24-hour cap is gone, so long-running goals no longer burn budg=
et while you are away. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/=
en/kimi-code-cli/guides/interaction.html#goal-mode">Goal mode</a></p><p>Als=
o in this release: <code>kimi upgrade</code> (alias <code>kimi update</code=
>) gains a <code>-y, --yes</code> flag to skip the confirmation prompt; the=
 new <code>KIMI_CODE_PERMISSION_MODE_REMINDER</code> environment variable (=
set to <code>0</code>) stops injecting auto-permission-mode reminders into =
the model context. v0.43.1 fixes pressing <code>Ctrl-C</code> while a subag=
ent is running quitting the entire CLI =E2=80=94 it now only interrupts the=
 running subagent.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry wn-hero"><div clas=
s=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Model Release</span><h2 id=3D"k2-8=
-preview-september-11-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">K=
2.8 Preview</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">September 11, 2026</span> <a cla=
ss=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/wh=
ats-new.html#k2-8-preview-september-11-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=
=80=9CK2.8 Preview September 11, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><di=
v class=3D"wn-content"><p>=F0=9F=8E=89 <strong>K2.8 Preview</strong> is now=
 fully rolled out in Kimi Code! The Model ID is unchanged =E2=80=94 still <=
code>kimi-for-coding</code> =E2=80=94 so clients and third-party tools work=
 with no configuration changes. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/c=
ode/docs/en/kimi-code/models.html">Model configuration</a></p><h4 id=3D"per=
formance-close-to-k3-with-more-efficient-thinking" tabindex=3D"-1">Performa=
nce close to K3, with more efficient thinking <a class=3D"header-anchor" hr=
ef=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#performanc=
e-close-to-k3-with-more-efficient-thinking" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=
=80=9CPerformance close to K3, with more efficient thinking=E2=80=9D">=E2=
=80=8B</a></h4><p>Coding and agent capabilities are improved across the boa=
rd, with significantly more efficient thinking than K2.7 Code.</p><h4 id=3D=
"adjustable-thinking-effort" tabindex=3D"-1">Adjustable thinking effort <a =
class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code=
/whats-new.html#adjustable-thinking-effort" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=
=80=9CAdjustable thinking effort=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Same thinki=
ng levels as K3: <code>low</code> / <code>high</code> / <code>max</code> (d=
efault <code>max</code>). With thinking turned off, requests to the K3 seri=
es and K2.8 Preview are served by K2.8 Preview (no thinking).</p><h4 id=3D"=
_1m-ultra-long-context" tabindex=3D"-1">1M ultra-long context <a class=3D"h=
eader-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new=
.html#_1m-ultra-long-context" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9C1M ultra-=
long context=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>A context window of up to 1M is=
 available across all membership tiers.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-ent=
ry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><=
h2 id=3D"v0-42-0-september-9-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-he=
ader">v0.42.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">September 9, 2026</span> <a cl=
ass=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/w=
hats-new.html#v0-42-0-september-9-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=
=9Cv0.42.0 September 9, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=
=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"remote-control-is-now-generally-available" tabind=
ex=3D"-1">Remote Control is now generally available <a class=3D"header-anch=
or" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#remo=
te-control-is-now-generally-available" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9C=
Remote Control is now generally available=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Re=
mote Control is out of the experimental stage =E2=80=94 no experimental fla=
g needed. Take over a local session from your phone or another computer, an=
ywhere. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cl=
i/guides/remote-control.html">Remote Control</a></p><h4 id=3D"sortable-medi=
a-preview-bar-in-the-web-input-box" tabindex=3D"-1">Sortable media preview =
bar in the Web input box <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kim=
i.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#sortable-media-preview-bar-in-t=
he-web-input-box" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CSortable media previe=
w bar in the Web input box=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Attachments appea=
r in a sortable preview bar, so you can reference images and videos inline =
in your text, and previews survive queuing and sending. HEIC, HEIF, and BMP=
 images are now supported too. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/co=
de/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/guides/interaction.html#pasting-images-and-video">=
Pasting images and video</a></p><h4 id=3D"completed-tool-calls-collapse-int=
o-summaries" tabindex=3D"-1">Completed tool calls collapse into summaries <=
a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-co=
de/whats-new.html#completed-tool-calls-collapse-into-summaries" aria-label=
=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CCompleted tool calls collapse into summaries=E2=
=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Finished tool calls now collapse into a title =
plus a one-line result summary, keeping the transcript clean =E2=80=94 pres=
s <code>Ctrl-O</code> to expand the full output. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https=
://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/reference/keyboard.html#tool-out=
put">Keyboard shortcuts</a></p><p>Also in this release: the <code>/btw</cod=
e> side-chat subagent gains read-only tools; the subagent model pool (<code=
>[secondary_model]</code>) is now always on and its experimental flag has b=
een removed.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta">=
<span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-41-0-september-=
4-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.41.0</span> <span =
class=3D"wn-date">September 4, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-41-0-sept=
ember-4-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.41.0 September 4, 2026=
=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"towe=
r-multi-agent-collaboration-in-web" tabindex=3D"-1">Tower multi-agent colla=
boration in Web <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/cod=
e/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#tower-multi-agent-collaboration-in-web" =
aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CTower multi-agent collaboration in Web=
=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The web version adds an experimental tower =
multi-agent mode =E2=80=94 enable it with the <code>/tower</code> command o=
r the plus menu in the input box, and set the base branch with <code>/tower=
 &lt;base-branch&gt;</code>.</p><h4 id=3D"text-selection-annotations-in-web=
" tabindex=3D"-1">Text selection annotations in Web <a class=3D"header-anch=
or" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#text=
-selection-annotations-in-web" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CText sel=
ection annotations in Web=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Select text in mes=
sages, file previews, diff and per-turn change panels, or the terminal to a=
dd a comment or quote it into the conversation.</p><h4 id=3D"dangerous-comm=
ands-no-longer-blocked" tabindex=3D"-1">Dangerous commands no longer blocke=
d <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi=
-code/whats-new.html#dangerous-commands-no-longer-blocked" aria-label=3D"Pe=
rmalink to =E2=80=9CDangerous commands no longer blocked=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=
=8B</a></h4><p>Auto permission mode no longer blocks dangerous commands or =
commands that cannot be statically analyzed. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://w=
ww.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/guides/interaction.html#the-three-pe=
rmission-modes">The three permission modes</a></p><p>Also in this release: =
a new session rating prompt (can be disabled in config); answers to backgro=
und questions are now delivered directly to the agent instead of through an=
 output file.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"=
><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-40-0-september=
-2-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.40.0</span> <span=
 class=3D"wn-date">September 2, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-40-0-sept=
ember-2-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.40.0 September 2, 2026=
=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"rena=
med-permission-modes-and-a-new-dangerous-command-guard" tabindex=3D"-1">Ren=
amed permission modes and a new dangerous-command guard <a class=3D"header-=
anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#=
renamed-permission-modes-and-a-new-dangerous-command-guard" aria-label=3D"P=
ermalink to =E2=80=9CRenamed permission modes and a new dangerous-command g=
uard=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The former YOLO / Auto modes are now As=
k When Needed (<code>/ask-when-needed</code>) and Never Ask (<code>/never-a=
sk</code>); Manual is Always Ask. A built-in dangerous-command guard also s=
hips in this release: commands such as <code>shutdown</code>, <code>reboot<=
/code>, or <code>rm -rf</code> are blocked outright in Never Ask mode and a=
lways require your confirmation in the other modes; disable it with <code>[=
permission] dangerous_command_guard =3D false</code>. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"=
https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/guides/interaction.html#the=
-three-permission-modes">Interaction &amp; input</a></p><h4 id=3D"subagent-=
model-pool-graduates-from-experimental" tabindex=3D"-1">Subagent model pool=
 graduates from experimental <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www=
.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#subagent-model-pool-graduat=
es-from-experimental" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CSubagent model po=
ol graduates from experimental=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The <code>[se=
condary_model]</code> subagent settings are now generally available and ena=
bled by default in every launch mode; you can still opt out with <code>KIMI=
_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_SECONDARY_MODEL=3D0</code> or <code>[experimental] secon=
dary-model =3D false</code>. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code=
/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configuration/config-files.html#secondary-model">Con=
fig files</a></p><h4 id=3D"plugins-panel-in-web-settings" tabindex=3D"-1">P=
lugins panel in web settings <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www=
.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#plugins-panel-in-web-settin=
gs" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CPlugins panel in web settings=E2=80=
=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The web settings now include a Plugins panel for =
browsing the plugin marketplace and installing, enabling, disabling, or rem=
oving plugins. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-=
code-cli/customization/plugins.html">Plugins</a></p><p>Also in this release=
: Tower mode (experimental) no longer starts on its own =E2=80=94 turn it o=
n explicitly with <code>/tower on</code> or <code>/tower &lt;base-branch&gt=
;</code>; the new <code>kimi session list</code> command lists sessions fro=
m the command line. v0.40.1 fixes the kimi-cli migration prompt reappearing=
 after the migration had completed or been dismissed.</p></div></div><div c=
lass=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Co=
de CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-39-0-august-27-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=
=3D"ignore-header">v0.39.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">August 27, 2026</=
span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/=
kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-39-0-august-27-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to=
 =E2=80=9Cv0.39.0 August 27, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div cl=
ass=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"remote-control-for-local-web-sessions" tabinde=
x=3D"-1">Remote control for local web sessions <a class=3D"header-anchor" h=
ref=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#remote-co=
ntrol-for-local-web-sessions" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CRemote co=
ntrol for local web sessions=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Set <code>KIMI_=
CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_REMOTE_CONTROL=3D1</code>, then run <code>kimi rc</code>,=
 <code>kimi web --remote-control</code>, or <code>/remote-control</code> to=
 access a local web session remotely. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi=
.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/guides/remote-control.html">Remote control<=
/a></p><h4 id=3D"experimental-tower-multi-agent-orchestration" tabindex=3D"=
-1">Experimental Tower multi-agent orchestration <a class=3D"header-anchor"=
 href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#experim=
ental-tower-multi-agent-orchestration" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9C=
Experimental Tower multi-agent orchestration=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p=
>Set <code>KIMI_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_TOWER=3D1</code>, then use <code>/tower o=
n</code> and <code>/tower &lt;objective&gt;</code> to start Tower mode and =
coordinate multiple agents toward an objective.</p><h4 id=3D"fork-subagents=
-from-the-current-conversation" tabindex=3D"-1">Fork subagents from the cur=
rent conversation <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/c=
ode/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#fork-subagents-from-the-current-conver=
sation" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CFork subagents from the current=
 conversation=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Set <code>KIMI_CODE_EXPERIMENT=
AL_SUBAGENT_FORK=3D1</code>, or <code>subagent_fork =3D true</code> under <=
code>[experimental]</code>, to let the subagent and swarm tools use <code>f=
ork</code> to start from a snapshot of the calling agent's conversation his=
tory. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/=
customization/agents.html">Agents and subagents</a></p><p>Also in this rele=
ase: Configure an independent AgentSwarm timeout with <code>[swarm] timeout=
_ms</code> or <code>KIMI_CODE_SWARM_TIMEOUT_MS</code>; file tools and Shell=
 now resolve Git Bash paths correctly on Windows. v0.39.1 fixes the web per=
mission mode leaking across sessions, the first typed character being swall=
owed in an empty composer, and startup hanging on "Connecting=E2=80=A6" wit=
h many workspaces, and adds a file mode to the OpenIn menu.</p></div></div>=
<div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">K=
imi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-38-0-august-20-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span =
class=3D"ignore-header">v0.38.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">August 20, 2=
026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/doc=
s/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-38-0-august-20-2026" aria-label=3D"Permali=
nk to =E2=80=9Cv0.38.0 August 20, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><d=
iv class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"new-waitfor-tool" tabindex=3D"-1">New Wai=
tFor tool <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs=
/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#new-waitfor-tool" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =
=E2=80=9CNew WaitFor tool=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The agent can now =
wait for a background task to finish within the current turn =E2=80=94 no n=
eed to end the turn and get woken up again. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://ww=
w.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/reference/tools.html#background-tasks=
">Background Tasks</a></p><h4 id=3D"_13-new-data-sources-in-kimi-datasource=
" tabindex=3D"-1">13 new data sources in Kimi Datasource <a class=3D"header=
-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html=
#_13-new-data-sources-in-kimi-datasource" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=
=9C13 new data sources in Kimi Datasource=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Th=
e official data plugin adds Chinese government data (NDA/NBS) and standards=
 (GB/HB/DB/TT), eight international organization datasets (WHO, FAO, UNSD, =
ECB, Eurostat, UNICEF, OECD, FRED), Xinhua Finance, and Caixin. Update the =
plugin from the Official tab in <code>/plugins</code>. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D=
"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/customization/plugins.html=
#kimi-datasource">Kimi Datasource</a></p><p>Also in this release: Edit and =
Write now require reading an existing file before modifying it; overly long=
 <code>!</code> shell command output is collapsed automatically =E2=80=94 p=
ress ctrl+o to expand it together with tool output.</p></div></div><div cla=
ss=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code=
