.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#subagent-model-pool" aria-label=
=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CSubagent model pool=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><=
p>The experimental subagent model configuration is now a model pool: list c=
andidate models with descriptions under <code>[secondary_model]</code>, and=
 the main agent picks one per spawn based on the task; you can also pin a d=
efault with <code>/secondary-model</code> or <code>default_model</code>. En=
able it with <code>KIMI_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_SECONDARY_MODEL=3D1</code>. =E2=
=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configura=
tion/config-files.html#subagent-model-pool">Subagent model pool</a></p><h4 =
id=3D"experimental-fullscreen-tui-mode" tabindex=3D"-1">Experimental fullsc=
reen TUI mode <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/=
docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#experimental-fullscreen-tui-mode" aria-lab=
el=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CExperimental fullscreen TUI mode=E2=80=9D">=E2=
=80=8B</a></h4><p>Set <code>KIMI_CODE_TUI_FULL_SCREEN=3D1</code> to switch =
to a fullscreen alternate-screen UI: scrollable transcript viewport, mouse =
text selection, clickable links, and Ctrl-Shift-F search. =E2=86=92 <a href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configuration/env-vars.=
html">Environment Variables</a></p><h4 id=3D"latex-math-rendering" tabindex=
=3D"-1">LaTeX math rendering <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www=
.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#latex-math-rendering" aria-=
label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CLaTeX math rendering=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a>=
</h4><p>The TUI now renders LaTeX math formulas (<code>$=E2=80=A6$</code> /=
 <code>$$=E2=80=A6$$</code>) in messages as Unicode formulas.</p><p>Also in=
 this release: the workspace trust prompt now shows project MCP launch targ=
ets and defaults to declining trust, and untrusted workspaces can no longer=
 plant same-named <code>fd</code>/<code>stty</code> executables; fixed Ctrl=
+C being ignored during automatic retries of failed API requests.</p></div>=
</div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-prod=
uct">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-35-0-august-12-2026" tabindex=3D"-1">=
<span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.35.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">August=
 12, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/co=
de/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-35-0-august-12-2026" aria-label=3D"P=
ermalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.35.0 August 12, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></=
div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"modern-web-guidance-plugin-in-the-b=
undled-marketplace" tabindex=3D"-1">Modern Web Guidance plugin in the bundl=
ed marketplace <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code=
/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#modern-web-guidance-plugin-in-the-bundled=
-marketplace" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CModern Web Guidance plugi=
n in the bundled marketplace=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Run <code>/plug=
ins</code> and select Modern Web Guidance to install it and get modern web =
development guidance. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/e=
n/kimi-code-cli/customization/plugins.html">Plugins</a></p><h4 id=3D"live-b=
ackground-subagent-progress-in-the-tasks-panel" tabindex=3D"-1">Live backgr=
ound-subagent progress in the <code>/tasks</code> panel <a class=3D"header-=
anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#=
live-background-subagent-progress-in-the-tasks-panel" aria-label=3D"Permali=
nk to =E2=80=9CLive background-subagent progress in the /tasks panel=E2=80=
=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The <code>/tasks</code> panel now shows the live =
work progress of background subagents, so you can follow along without wait=
ing for them to finish. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs=
/en/kimi-code-cli/reference/slash-commands.html">Slash Commands</a></p><p>A=
lso in this release: fixed the token counts reported after compaction readi=
ng far below the real context size =E2=80=94 they now match the numbers sho=
wn while the session runs; fixed coder subagents spawning further subagents=
 by default.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta">=
<span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-34-0-august-6-2=
026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.34.0</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"wn-date">August 6, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"htt=
ps://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-34-0-august-6-20=
26" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.34.0 August 6, 2026=E2=80=9D">=
=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"kimi-computer-u=
se-comes-to-windows" tabindex=3D"-1">Kimi Computer Use comes to Windows <a =
class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code=
/whats-new.html#kimi-computer-use-comes-to-windows" aria-label=3D"Permalink=
 to =E2=80=9CKimi Computer Use comes to Windows=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4=
><p>Kimi Computer Use now supports Windows x64 (Windows 10 1903+ / Windows =
11) =E2=80=94 install it from the Official tab in <code>/plugins</code>. =
=E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/custom=
ization/plugins.html#kimi-computer-use">Kimi Computer Use</a></p><h4 id=3D"=
cache-expiry-reminder" tabindex=3D"-1">Cache-expiry reminder <a class=3D"he=
ader-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.=
html#cache-expiry-reminder" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CCache-expir=
y reminder=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Resuming a long-idle session or s=
ending a message after a long idle stretch now shows a reminder that the co=
ntext cache may have expired, with options to compact or start a new sessio=
n first; set <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/con=
figuration/config-files.html#tui-toml"><code>cache_expiry_hint</code></a> t=
o <code>false</code> to disable it.</p><h4 id=3D"kimi-web-stability-and-exp=
erience-improvements" tabindex=3D"-1"><code>kimi web</code> stability and e=
xperience improvements <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.=
com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#kimi-web-stability-and-experience=
-improvements" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Ckimi web stability and e=
xperience improvements=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>When a model request =
fails, a failure card now stays in the session with one-click resume; the s=
idebar session list adds a flat view; subagent tasks show the model and thi=
nking level they use; and the working status shows retry progress (attempt =
N of M) during automatic retries.</p><p>Also in this release: browser exten=
sion links and activation steps are shown after installing Kimi WebBridge; =
UTF-16 text files can now be read; <code>/feedback</code> works for all sig=
ned-in users; fixed <code>kimi -p</code> exiting before background tasks an=
d subagents finish; fixed removing an MCP server breaking open sessions (it=
s tools stay visible, but calls fail with a removal notice).</p></div></div=
><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">=
Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-33-0-august-5-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span =
class=3D"ignore-header">v0.33.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">August 5, 20=
26</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs=
/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-33-0-august-5-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink=
 to =E2=80=9Cv0.33.0 August 5, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div =
class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"official-built-in-plugins-kimi-computer-use-=
and-kimi-webbridge" tabindex=3D"-1">Official built-in plugins: Kimi Compute=
r Use and Kimi WebBridge <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kim=
i.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#official-built-in-plugins-kimi-=
computer-use-and-kimi-webbridge" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9COffici=
al built-in plugins: Kimi Computer Use and Kimi WebBridge=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=
=8B</a></h4><p>The Official tab of the <code>/plugins</code> marketplace no=
w lists two official built-in capabilities =E2=80=94 press Enter to deploy =
the managed runtime in one step, with retry after interrupted installs and =
automatic backup of legacy WebBridge skills on upgrade. =E2=86=92 <a href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/customization/plugins.h=
tml#installation-and-management">Installation and Management</a></p><h4 id=
=3D"agent-core-v2-engine-enabled-by-default" tabindex=3D"-1">agent-core-v2 =
engine enabled by default <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.ki=
mi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#agent-core-v2-engine-enabled-b=
y-default" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cagent-core-v2 engine enabled=
 by default=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The interactive TUI, <code>kimi =
-p</code>, <code>kimi acp</code>, and other CLI surfaces now run on the age=
nt-core-v2 engine by default; set <code>KIMI_CODE_LEGACY_FLAG=3D1</code> to=
 fall back to the legacy engine if needed. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www=
.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configuration/env-vars.html">Environme=
nt Variables</a></p><h4 id=3D"kimi-web-enhancements" tabindex=3D"-1"><code>=
kimi web</code> enhancements <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www=
.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#kimi-web-enhancements" aria=
-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Ckimi web enhancements=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</=
a></h4><p>The web UI now supports adding and managing custom providers in s=
ettings, pinning sessions in the sidebar, setting emoji session titles, and=
 viewing your signed-in account and plan usage.</p><p>Also in this release:=
 new <code>/bug</code> command as an alias for <code>/feedback</code>; star=
tup now asks whether to trust the current folder; fixed MCP OAuth re-author=
ization always failing with <code>Invalid redirect URI</code>.</p></div></d=
iv><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product=
">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-32-0-august-4-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><spa=
n class=3D"ignore-header">v0.32.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">August 4, =
2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/do=
cs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-32-0-august-4-2026" aria-label=3D"Permali=
nk to =E2=80=9Cv0.32.0 August 4, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><di=
v class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"four-new-hook-events" tabindex=3D"-1">Four=
 new hook events <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/co=
de/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#four-new-hook-events" aria-label=3D"Per=
malink to =E2=80=9CFour new hook events=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Four=
 new hook events =E2=80=94 <code>TurnStarted</code>, <code>UserPromptQueued=
</code>, <code>TaskStarted</code>, and <code>SessionHeartbeat</code> =E2=80=
=94 let you observe turn starts, queued user input, sub-task launches, and =
session heartbeats by configuring them under <code>[[hooks]]</code> in <cod=
e>config.toml</code>. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/e=
n/kimi-code-cli/customization/hooks.html#event-reference">Event Reference</=
a></p><h4 id=3D"loop-control-config-keys-renamed" tabindex=3D"-1"><code>loo=
p_control</code> config keys renamed <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"htt=
ps://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#loop-control-config=
-keys-renamed" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cloop_control config keys=
 renamed=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p><code>max_retries_per_step</code> i=
s now <code>max_attempts_per_step</code>, and <code>max_steps_per_run</code=
> is now <code>max_steps_per_turn</code>. The old keys no longer take effec=
t =E2=80=94 a rename warning is shown at startup, so update your config. =
=E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/config=
uration/config-files.html#loop-control">loop_control</a></p><h4 id=3D"local=
-token-usage-estimation" tabindex=3D"-1">Local token-usage estimation <a cl=
ass=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/w=
hats-new.html#local-token-usage-estimation" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=
=80=9CLocal token-usage estimation=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>A new <co=
de>[token_counting]</code> config section: when the provider doesn't report=
 token usage, the context-size display can switch to a local estimate. =E2=
=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configura=
tion/config-files.html#token-counting">token_counting</a></p><p>Also in thi=
s release: when the models.dev catalog is unreachable, Kimi Code falls back=
 to a built-in snapshot so known third-party providers can still be importe=
d offline; fixed auto-compaction retrying an oversized request until failur=
e.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span clas=
s=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-31-0-july-30-2026" tabind=
ex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.31.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-da=
te">July 30, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kim=
i.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-31-0-july-30-2026" aria-labe=
l=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.31.0 July 30, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h=
2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"plugins-can-contribute-custom-a=
gents" tabindex=3D"-1">Plugins can contribute custom agents <a class=3D"hea=
der-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.h=
tml#plugins-can-contribute-custom-agents" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=
=9CPlugins can contribute custom agents=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>A pl=
ugin can now ship its own agents: declare directories in the manifest's <co=
de>agents</code> field, or simply place an <code>agents/</code> directory a=
t the plugin root. The agent files are discovered automatically while the p=
lugin is enabled and are available for sub-agent delegation. =E2=86=92 <a h=
ref=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/customization/plugin=
s.html#plugin-agents">Plugin Agents</a></p><h4 id=3D"plugins-can-inject-sys=
tem-prompt-instructions" tabindex=3D"-1">Plugins can inject system-prompt i=
nstructions <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/do=
cs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#plugins-can-inject-system-prompt-instruction=
s" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CPlugins can inject system-prompt ins=
tructions=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p><code>kimi.plugin.json</code> gain=
s <code>systemPrompt</code> and <code>systemPromptPath</code> fields, letti=
ng an enabled plugin contribute instructions to the agent's system prompt =
=E2=80=94 effective in the TUI, <code>kimi -p</code>, and <code>kimi web</c=
ode>. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/=
customization/plugins.html#system-prompt-instructions">System-prompt instru=
ctions</a></p><h4 id=3D"markdown-defined-custom-agents-in-the-tui" tabindex=
=3D"-1">Markdown-defined custom agents in the TUI <a class=3D"header-anchor=
" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#markdo=
wn-defined-custom-agents-in-the-tui" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CMa=
rkdown-defined custom agents in the TUI=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Mark=
down agent files, previously limited to <code>kimi web</code>, now work in =
the TUI as well: frontmatter declares the name, description, and tool permi=
ssions, and the body is the system prompt. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www=
.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/customization/agents.html#custom-agent=
s">Custom Agents</a></p><p>Also in this release: the new <code>/secondary_m=
odel</code> slash command configures the secondary model used by sub-agents=
 (experimental =E2=80=94 enable it in <code>/experiments</code> first); Tas=
kOutput is now always non-blocking, returning an immediate snapshot while c=
ompletion still arrives via automatic notification.</p></div></div><div cla=
ss=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code=
 CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-30-0-july-29-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"i=
