a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-co=
de/whats-new.html#v0-30-0-july-29-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=
=9Cv0.30.0 July 29, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn=
-content"><h4 id=3D"customizable-footer-status-line" tabindex=3D"-1">Custom=
izable footer status line <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.ki=
mi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#customizable-footer-status-lin=
e" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CCustomizable footer status line=E2=
=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p><code>tui.toml</code> gains a <code>[status_li=
ne]</code> section: arrange the built-in slots (mode, goal, model, tasks, g=
it, and more) with <code>items</code>, or plug in your own status-line comm=
and with <code>command</code>. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/co=
de/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configuration/config-files.html#tui-toml">Configur=
ation files</a></p><h4 id=3D"fail-fast-when-quota-runs-out" tabindex=3D"-1"=
>Fail fast when quota runs out <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://w=
ww.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#fail-fast-when-quota-runs=
-out" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CFail fast when quota runs out=E2=
=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>When your account quota or balance is exhauste=
d, Kimi Code now errors immediately instead of silently retrying for about =
3 minutes.</p><p>Also in this release: installing an official plugin that b=
ills against plan quota (like Kimi Datasource) now shows a quota note, and =
you're nudged to run <code>/plugins</code> when a plugin used in the sessio=
n has an update; repeated invalid tool calls now stop the turn instead of r=
etrying indefinitely.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"=
wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-29-1-j=
uly-24-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.29.1</span> <=
span class=3D"wn-date">July 24, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-29-1-july=
-24-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.29.1 July 24, 2026=E2=80=
=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"web-search=
-and-web-fetch-without-oauth" tabindex=3D"-1">Web search and web fetch with=
out OAuth <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs=
/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#web-search-and-web-fetch-without-oauth" aria-l=
abel=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CWeb search and web fetch without OAuth=E2=80=
=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>v0.29.1 adds <code>KIMI_WEB_SEARCH_*</code> and <=
code>KIMI_WEB_FETCH_*</code> environment variables so you can configure web=
 search and web fetch services without OAuth login. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"ht=
tps://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configuration/env-vars.html#r=
untime-switches">Environment variables</a></p><h4 id=3D"global-default-mcp-=
server-timeouts" tabindex=3D"-1">Global default MCP server timeouts <a clas=
s=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/wha=
ts-new.html#global-default-mcp-server-timeouts" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =
=E2=80=9CGlobal default MCP server timeouts=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>=
<code>config.toml</code> and environment variables now support global defau=
lt MCP server timeouts, so you don't have to set them per server. =E2=86=92=
 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configuration/c=
onfig-files.html#mcp">Configuration files</a></p><p>Also in this release: e=
xperimental secondary-model bindings for newly spawned subagents; fix loss =
of thinking content with OpenAI-compatible endpoints that return reasoning =
under a different field name.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div c=
lass=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v=
0-29-0-july-22-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.29.0<=
/span> <span class=3D"wn-date">July 22, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anch=
or" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-2=
9-0-july-22-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.29.0 July 22, 2026=
=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"web-=
define-agents-with-markdown-files" tabindex=3D"-1">Web: Define agents with =
Markdown files <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code=
/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#web-define-agents-with-markdown-files" ar=
ia-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CWeb: Define agents with Markdown files=E2=
=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>You can now define your own agents as Markdown=
 files: frontmatter at the top declares name, description, and tool permiss=
ions, and the body is the system prompt. Custom agents are discovered autom=
atically by the main agent and delegated alongside built-in sub-agents. =E2=
=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/customiza=
tion/agents.html#custom-agents">Agents and Sub-Agents</a></p><h4 id=3D"web-=
system-md-overrides-the-main-agent-s-system-prompt" tabindex=3D"-1">Web: SY=
STEM.md overrides the main agent's system prompt <a class=3D"header-anchor"=
 href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#web-sys=
tem-md-overrides-the-main-agent-s-system-prompt" aria-label=3D"Permalink to=
 =E2=80=9CWeb: SYSTEM.md overrides the main agent's system prompt=E2=80=9D"=
>=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Write a plain Markdown <code>$KIMI_CODE_HOME/SYSTEM.m=
d</code> to permanently override the default main agent's system prompt wit=
hout passing <code>--agent</code> or <code>--agent-file</code> every launch=
; explicitly passed agent files still take precedence. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D=
"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/customization/agents.html#=
overriding-the-main-agent-s-system-prompt-with-system-md">Agents and Sub-Ag=
ents</a></p><h4 id=3D"enable-disable-tools-globally-in-config-toml" tabinde=
x=3D"-1">Enable/disable tools globally in config.toml <a class=3D"header-an=
chor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#en=
able-disable-tools-globally-in-config-toml" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=
=80=9CEnable/disable tools globally in config.toml=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a><=
/h4><p>A new <code>[tools]</code> table in <code>config.toml</code> lets yo=
u enable or disable specific tools across all sessions, so you don't have t=
o adjust them manually each time. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com=
/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configuration/config-files.html#tools">Configur=
ation files</a></p><p>Also in this release: videos attached to prompts are =
now delivered to the model with the prompt itself; the ACP client supports =
choosing thinking effort; v0.29.1 adds environment variables for web search=
 and web fetch services without OAuth login, plus global default MCP server=
 timeouts in <code>config.toml</code>.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entr=
y"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h=
2 id=3D"v0-28-0-july-20-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header"=
