ader-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.=
html#v0-28-0-july-20-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.28.0 July=
 20, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 i=
d=3D"kimi-web-runs-in-the-foreground-kimi-server-deprecated" tabindex=3D"-1=
"><code>kimi web</code> runs in the foreground, <code>kimi server</code> de=
precated <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/=
en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#kimi-web-runs-in-the-foreground-kimi-server-dep=
recated" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Ckimi web runs in the foregroun=
d, kimi server deprecated=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p><code>kimi web</co=
de> now runs in the current terminal foreground and opens the browser autom=
atically; stop it with <code>Ctrl+C</code>. The old <code>kimi server</code=
> command tree is deprecated, its subcommands removed, with only <code>kimi=
 server kill</code> retained as a fallback for stopping background services=
 launched before v0.28.0. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/do=
cs/en/kimi-code-cli/reference/kimi-command.html#kimi-web">kimi web</a></p><=
h4 id=3D"thinking-effort-persists-more-conservatively" tabindex=3D"-1">Thin=
king effort persists more conservatively <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D=
"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#thinking-effort=
-persists-more-conservatively" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CThinking=
 effort persists more conservatively=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Thinkin=
g effort is now persisted only for levels below a model's top tier (<code>m=
ax</code>), so switching models no longer leaves you with an empty or unres=
ponsive effort picker when the old <code>max</code> setting isn't supported=
. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/conf=
iguration/config-files.html#models">Model configuration</a></p><p>Also in t=
his release: the web model switcher now warns that switching models or thin=
king effort invalidates the existing prompt cache; the YOLO and Auto permis=
sion mode descriptions are corrected =E2=80=94 YOLO auto-approves tool acti=
ons but may still ask questions, while Auto is fully autonomous and never a=
sks.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span cl=
ass=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-27-0-july-17-2026" tabi=
ndex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.27.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-=
date">July 17, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.k=
imi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-27-0-july-17-2026" aria-la=
bel=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.27.0 July 17, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a><=
/h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"copy-for-the-last-reply" tabi=
ndex=3D"-1"><code>/copy</code> for the last reply <a class=3D"header-anchor=
" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#copy-f=
or-the-last-reply" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9C/copy for the last r=
eply=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>New <code>/copy</code> slash command co=
pies the last assistant message to the clipboard =E2=80=94 no more manually=
 selecting long answers. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/doc=
s/en/kimi-code-cli/reference/slash-commands.html">Slash Commands</a></p><h4=
 id=3D"auto-refresh-of-the-model-list-for-api-key-users" tabindex=3D"-1">Au=
to-refresh of the model list for API key users <a class=3D"header-anchor" h=
ref=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#auto-refr=
esh-of-the-model-list-for-api-key-users" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=
=9CAuto-refresh of the model list for API key users=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a>=
</h4><p>When calling Kimi coding models with an API key, Kimi Code now auto=
matically fetches the latest model list, so new models are usable without m=
anual config changes. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/e=
n/kimi-code-cli/configuration/config-files.html#models">Model configuration=
</a></p><p>Also in this release: OAuth connection failures now show the und=
erlying network cause (DNS, refused connection, TLS, timeout) instead of a =
bare <code>fetch failed</code>; the built-in URL fetch tool's network safeg=
uards are hardened so crafted domains and redirect chains can no longer rea=
ch loopback or internal network services.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-e=
ntry wn-hero"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Model Relea=
se</span><h2 id=3D"kimi-k3-july-16-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ign=
ore-header">Kimi K3</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">July 16, 2026</span> <a =
class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code=
/whats-new.html#kimi-k3-july-16-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CK=
imi K3 July 16, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-con=
tent"><p><strong>Kimi K3</strong>, our most capable model to date, is now r=
eleased and open-sourced, and available in Kimi Code.</p><h4 id=3D"model-sc=
ale-architecture" tabindex=3D"-1">Model scale &amp; architecture <a class=
=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/what=
s-new.html#model-scale-architecture" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CMo=
del scale &amp; architecture=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>2.8 trillion pa=
rameters, built on KDA hybrid linear attention and Attention Residuals =E2=
=80=94 the first open-source model at the 3-trillion-parameter scale.</p><h=
4 id=3D"long-context-multimodal" tabindex=3D"-1">Long context &amp; multimo=
dal <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/ki=
mi-code/whats-new.html#long-context-multimodal" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =
=E2=80=9CLong context &amp; multimodal=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Nativ=
e visual understanding with up to 1M-token context, handling large codebase=
s and extended coherent reasoning.</p><h4 id=3D"coding-agent-strengths" tab=
index=3D"-1">Coding &amp; agent strengths <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#coding-agent=
-strengths" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CCoding &amp; agent strength=
s=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Excels at long-horizon programming, game d=
ev / 3D, and knowledge work; sustains long engineering tasks with minimal h=
uman supervision across kernel optimization, GPU compilers, chip design, an=
d scientific computing.</p><h4 id=3D"benchmark-positioning" tabindex=3D"-1"=
>Benchmark positioning <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.=
com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#benchmark-positioning" aria-label=
=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CBenchmark positioning=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4=
><p>A top-tier model that outperforms Opus 4.8, GPT 5.5, and other mainstre=
am models; on challenging coding tasks such as kernel optimization, it perf=
orms close to the strongest proprietary models.</p><h4 id=3D"membership" ta=
bindex=3D"-1">Membership <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kim=
i.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#membership" aria-label=3D"Perma=
link to =E2=80=9CMembership=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Moderato members=
 and above can use Kimi K3; Allegretto members and above unlock the 1M cont=
ext window. K3 now supports <code>low</code> / <code>high</code> / <code>ma=
x</code> thinking effort levels, so you can pick the right intensity for ea=
ch task. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/m=
odels.html">Model configuration</a></p><h4 id=3D"usage-tip" tabindex=3D"-1"=
>Usage tip <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/doc=
s/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#usage-tip" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=
=9CUsage tip=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Switching models invalidates th=
e existing context cache, so consumption is higher right after switching; s=
tart a new session before using Kimi K3 for better results and lower consum=
ption.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span =
class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-26-0-july-16-2026" ta=
bindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.26.0</span> <span class=3D"w=
n-date">July 16, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www=
.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-26-0-july-16-2026" aria-=
label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.26.0 July 16, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a=
></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"coder-sub-agent-capabilitie=
s-aligned-with-the-main-agent" tabindex=3D"-1">Coder sub-agent capabilities=
 aligned with the main agent <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www=
.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#coder-sub-agent-capabilitie=
s-aligned-with-the-main-agent" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CCoder su=
b-agent capabilities aligned with the main agent=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h=
4><p>The coder sub-agent now supports background tasks, todo lists, plan mo=
de, skill invocation, and nested agents, so it can handle more complex codi=
ng workflows on its own. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/doc=
s/en/kimi-code-cli/customization/agents.html">Agents and Sub-Agents</a></p>=
<h4 id=3D"cache-invalidation-hints-in-model-and-effort" tabindex=3D"-1">Cac=
he-invalidation hints in <code>/model</code> and <code>/effort</code> <a cl=
ass=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/w=
hats-new.html#cache-invalidation-hints-in-model-and-effort" aria-label=3D"P=
ermalink to =E2=80=9CCache-invalidation hints in /model and /effort=E2=80=
=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Switching the model or effort now warns that the =
existing prompt cache will be invalidated, and suggests using <code>/new</c=
ode> to avoid extra token costs. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/=
code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/reference/slash-commands.html">Slash Commands</a=
></p><p>Also in this release: the context-size indicator no longer under-re=
ports the model's actual context usage; a resumed session without new activ=
ity is no longer incorrectly marked as just updated.</p></div></div><div cl=
ass=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Cod=
e CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-25-0-july-16-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"=
ignore-header">v0.25.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">July 16, 2026</span> =
<a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-c=
ode/whats-new.html#v0-25-0-july-16-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=
=9Cv0.25.0 July 16, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn=
-content"><h4 id=3D"attach-any-file-in-web-chat" tabindex=3D"-1">Attach any=
 file in web chat <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/c=
ode/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#attach-any-file-in-web-chat" aria-labe=
l=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CAttach any file in web chat=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B<=
/a></h4><p>The built-in web UI now supports attaching files of any type in =
chat: drop a file anywhere on the window to send it, and files, images, and=
 videos are shown as attachment tags in the message bubble. =E2=86=92 <a hr=
ef=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/guides/ides.html">Usi=
ng Kimi Code CLI in IDEs</a></p><h4 id=3D"aligned-anthropic-effort-configur=
ation" tabindex=3D"-1">Aligned Anthropic effort configuration <a class=3D"h=
eader-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new=
.html#aligned-anthropic-effort-configuration" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =
=E2=80=9CAligned Anthropic effort configuration=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4=
><p>Anthropic-compatible providers now apply the official effort configurat=
ion, with unknown models falling back to a 128k output limit and custom-nam=
ed models getting correct thinking-strength controls for new sessions. =E2=
=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configura=
tion/providers.html">Providers and models</a></p><p>Also in this release: m=
odel request failures now show full diagnostics; two security issues were f=
ixed =E2=80=94 the web server's bearer-token check could be bypassed via pe=
rcent-encoded API paths, and the session filesystem API could follow symlin=
ks outside the workspace and access host files.</p></div></div><div class=
=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code C=
LI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-24-2-july-15-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ign=
ore-header">v0.24.2</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">July 15, 2026</span> <a =
class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code=
/whats-new.html#v0-24-2-july-15-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv=
0.24.2 July 15, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-con=
tent"><h4 id=3D"built-in-docs-q-a-skill" tabindex=3D"-1">Built-in docs Q&am=
p;A skill <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs=
/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#built-in-docs-q-a-skill" aria-label=3D"Permali=
nk to =E2=80=9CBuilt-in docs Q&amp;A skill=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>A=
 new built-in <code>/check-kimi-code-docs</code> answers Kimi Code product =
questions (CLI usage, configuration, membership, error codes) straight from=
 the official docs, citing source links in its answers =E2=80=94 so you no =
longer have to leave the terminal to look something up. =E2=86=92 <a href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/reference/slash-command=
s.html#built-in-skill-commands">Built-in Skill Commands</a></p><p>Also in t=
his release: the per-step LLM retry cap has been raised from 3 to 10, so tr=
ansient provider-side failures (429 / overload) are retried automatically b=
efore the whole turn fails; and print mode (<code>kimi -p</code>) no longer=
 exits after a single turn =E2=80=94 as long as background tasks are pendin=
g it stays alive and feeds each result back to the main agent (<code>print_=
background_mode</code> now defaults to <code>steer</code>, and background t=
asks and subagents no longer time out by default).</p></div></div><div clas=
s=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code =
CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-24-0-july-14-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ig=
nore-header">v0.24.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">July 14, 2026</span> <a=
 class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-cod=
e/whats-new.html#v0-24-0-july-14-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9C=
v0.24.0 July 14, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-co=
ntent"><h4 id=3D"session-export" tabindex=3D"-1">Session export <a class=3D=
"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-n=
ew.html#session-export" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CSession export=
=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The web UI can now export a session: run <c=
ode>/export</code>, or pick "Export session" from a session's overflow menu=
, to bundle the conversation and troubleshooting logs into a downloadable Z=
IP (up to 64 MiB) =E2=80=94 handy for archiving or filing a report. =E2=86=
=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/guides/sessi=
ons.html#exporting-a-session">Exporting a session</a></p><h4 id=3D"foregrou=
nd-commands-background-on-timeout" tabindex=3D"-1">Foreground commands back=
ground on timeout <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/c=
ode/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#foreground-commands-background-on-time=
out" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CForeground commands background on =
timeout=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>When a foreground <code>Bash</code> =
command hits its timeout it is no longer killed =E2=80=94 it moves to the b=
ackground and keeps running, reporting its result when it finishes, so long=
-running commands are no longer lost midway. Set <code>bash_auto_background=
_on_timeout =3D false</code> under <code>[background]</code> to restore the=
 kill-on-timeout behavior. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/d=
ocs/en/kimi-code-cli/reference/tools.html#shell">Built-in Tools =C2=B7 Shel=
l</a></p><p>Also in this release: forking a session now fully preserves med=
ia attachments, plan files, background task output, and cron jobs, and a fa=
iled fork no longer leaves a partial copy behind; <code>kimi web</code> now=
 defaults to the rebuilt agent engine.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entr=
y"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code</span><h2 id=
=3D"highspeed-extra-usage-are-live-july-9-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=
=3D"ignore-header">HighSpeed &amp; Extra Usage are live</span> <span class=
=3D"wn-date">July 9, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https:/=
/www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#highspeed-extra-usage-a=
re-live-july-9-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CHighSpeed &amp; Ex=
tra Usage are live July 9, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div clas=
s=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"=E2=9A=A1-highspeed-is-now-available" tabindex=
=3D"-1">=E2=9A=A1 HighSpeed is now available <a class=3D"header-anchor" hre=
f=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#%E2%9A%A1-h=
ighspeed-is-now-available" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9C=E2=9A=A1 Hi=
ghSpeed is now available=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Kimi Code now offer=
s two tiers =E2=80=94 <strong>Standard</strong> and <strong>HighSpeed</stro=
ng> =E2=80=94 built on the same model with identical coding ability; HighSp=
eed delivers roughly <strong>5=E2=80=936=C3=97 the output speed</strong> of=
 Standard. Switch instantly with <code>/model</code> in the CLI, or set the=
 model ID to <code>kimi-for-coding-highspeed</code> in third-party tools. H=
ighSpeed requires an <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/membership/pricing?fro=
m=3Dkfc_membership_topbar&amp;track_id=3Da7764d49-73ad-4d08-b2f3-a8d7433917=
f8" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">Allegretto</a> plan or above. =E2=
=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/models.html#s=
witch-model">How to Switch Models</a></p><h4 id=3D"extra-usage-is-now-avail=
able" tabindex=3D"-1">Extra Usage is now available <a class=3D"header-ancho=
r" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#extra=
-usage-is-now-available" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CExtra Usage is=
 now available=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>When your subscription quota =
runs out, keep making requests with your Extra Usage balance =E2=80=94 it <=
strong>bypasses the monthly / weekly / hourly membership quota limits</stro=
ng>, works whenever any limit is reached, only deducts the Extra Usage bala=
nce, and doesn't affect your membership quota refresh. Only subscribed memb=
ers can enable it, at Kimi homepage =E2=86=92 Settings =E2=86=92 Membership=
 Plan =E2=86=92 My Quota. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/do=
cs/en/kimi-code/membership.html#extra-usage">About Extra Usage</a></p></div=
></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-pro=
duct">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-23-0-july-6-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><s=
pan class=3D"ignore-header">v0.23.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">July 6, =
2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/do=
cs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-23-0-july-6-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink=
 to =E2=80=9Cv0.23.0 July 6, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div cl=
ass=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"archived-sessions" tabindex=3D"-1">Archived se=
ssions <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en=
/kimi-code/whats-new.html#archived-sessions" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=
=80=9CArchived sessions=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The web UI adds an A=
rchived sessions page where you can browse and restore archived sessions in=
 one click =E2=80=94 open Settings =E2=86=92 Archived to view them.</p><h4 =
id=3D"reasoning-preserved-across-turns" tabindex=3D"-1">Reasoning preserved=
 across turns <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/=
docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#reasoning-preserved-across-turns" aria-lab=
el=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CReasoning preserved across turns=E2=80=9D">=E2=
=80=8B</a></h4><p>With Thinking enabled, Kimi models now keep their reasoni=
ng across turns by default so the model can build on its earlier thought; s=
et <code>[thinking] keep =3D "off"</code> to disable it. =E2=86=92 <a href=
=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/configuration/config-fi=
les.html#thinking">Model configuration</a></p><h4 id=3D"compaction-summary-=
at-a-glance" tabindex=3D"-1">Compaction summary at a glance <a class=3D"hea=
der-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.h=
tml#compaction-summary-at-a-glance" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CCom=
paction summary at a glance=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>After the contex=
t is compacted, the TUI shows a summary of what was compacted; press <code>=
Ctrl-O</code> to show or hide it within the compaction block =E2=80=94 the =
same shortcut that collapses tool output. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.=
kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/guides/interaction.html#during-streamin=
g-output">Interaction and input</a></p><p>Also in this release: an experime=
ntal on-demand tool loader (<code>select_tools</code>) =E2=80=94 with the <=
code>tool-select</code> flag enabled, capable models load MCP tools on dema=
nd instead of sending them all on every request, preserving the provider's =
prompt cache; and sessions that existed on disk but were missing from the l=
ist or returned 404 on direct access are fixed, as the server now rebuilds =
the session index on startup.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div c=
lass=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v=
0-22-0-july-2-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.22.0</=
span> <span class=3D"wn-date">July 2, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor=
" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-22-=
0-july-2-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.22.0 July 2, 2026=E2=
=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"automat=
ic-oversized-image-compression" tabindex=3D"-1">Automatic oversized-image c=
ompression <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/doc=
s/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#automatic-oversized-image-compression" aria-l=
abel=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CAutomatic oversized-image compression=E2=80=
=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Images that exceed model limits are now automatic=
ally downsampled and re-encoded before reaching the model, cutting vision-t=
oken cost and avoiding provider image-size errors.</p><h4 id=3D"model-confi=
guration-overrides" tabindex=3D"-1">Model configuration overrides <a class=
=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/what=
s-new.html#model-configuration-overrides" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=
=9CModel configuration overrides=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>A new <code=
>[models."&lt;alias&gt;".overrides]</code> table lets you override model me=
tadata after provider-catalog refreshes =E2=80=94 useful for pinning thinki=
ng-effort levels, default effort, and other fields so custom configs surviv=
e refreshes. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-co=
de-cli/configuration/config-files.html#model-overrides">Model configuration=
</a></p><h4 id=3D"new-web-ui-design-system" tabindex=3D"-1">New web UI desi=
gn system <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs=
/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#new-web-ui-design-system" aria-label=3D"Permal=
ink to =E2=80=9CNew web UI design system=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The=
 built-in web UI gets a refreshed design system with updated colors, typogr=
aphy, spacing, light and dark palettes, and subtler enter/exit and expand/c=
ollapse animations for a more consistent look and feel.</p><p>Also in this =
release: a new Cmd/Ctrl+K session-search palette filters by title, workspac=
e, and recent prompt; consecutive tool calls are now grouped into a collaps=
ible stack with diff line counts and inline previews for image, video, and =
audio results.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta=
"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-21-0-july-1-2=
026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.21.0</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"wn-date">July 1, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https=
://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-21-0-july-1-2026" =
aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.21.0 July 1, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=
=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"plugins-can-provide-s=
lash-commands" tabindex=3D"-1">Plugins can provide slash commands <a class=
=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/what=
s-new.html#plugins-can-provide-slash-commands" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =
=E2=80=9CPlugins can provide slash commands=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>=
Plugins can now declare slash commands via a <code>commands</code> field in=
 their manifest, registered as <code>&lt;plugin&gt;:&lt;command&gt;</code> =
and invoked with <code>$ARGUMENTS</code> expansion =E2=80=94 turning common=
 workflows into commands with no extra setup. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://=
www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/customization/plugins.html#plugin-s=
lash-commands">Plugin slash commands</a></p><h4 id=3D"mermaid-diagrams-in-w=
eb-chat" tabindex=3D"-1">Mermaid diagrams in web chat <a class=3D"header-an=
chor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#me=
rmaid-diagrams-in-web-chat" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CMermaid dia=
grams in web chat=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Fenced <code>mermaid</code=
> blocks in assistant responses now render as diagrams in the built-in web =
UI, and KaTeX math and Mermaid parsing run in Web Workers to keep the UI re=
sponsive during live streaming.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div=
 class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D=
"v0-20-2-june-29-2026" tabindex=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.20.=
2</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">June 29, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-an=
chor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0=
-20-2-june-29-2026" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.20.2 June 29, 20=
26=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"vi=
deo-input-and-anthropic-compatible-protocol" tabindex=3D"-1">Video input an=
d Anthropic-compatible protocol <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://=
www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#video-input-and-anthropi=
c-compatible-protocol" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CVideo input and =
Anthropic-compatible protocol=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Kimi Code now =
supports the Anthropic-compatible protocol, and the <code>ReadMediaFile</co=
de> tool can send video to the model as multimodal content =E2=80=94 availa=
bility follows the current model's <code>image_in</code> / <code>video_in</=
code> capabilities. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/=
kimi-code-cli/reference/tools.html#file-tools">Built-in tools</a></p><h4 id=
=3D"web-completion-sound-and-notifications" tabindex=3D"-1">Web completion =
sound and notifications <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi=
.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#web-completion-sound-and-notific=
ations" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CWeb completion sound and notifi=
cations=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>The built-in web UI gains a completi=
on sound, a completion notification, and an issue notification, each with i=
ts own toggle in settings. Issue notifications are off by default; only aft=
er you opt in is the issue text pushed to the desktop.</p><h4 id=3D"custom-=
outbound-request-headers" tabindex=3D"-1">Custom outbound request headers <=
a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-co=
de/whats-new.html#custom-outbound-request-headers" aria-label=3D"Permalink =
to =E2=80=9CCustom outbound request headers=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>=
A new <code>KIMI_CODE_CUSTOM_HEADERS</code> environment variable lets you c=
ustomize headers on outbound LLM requests (one <code>Name: Value</code> per=
 line), and a <code>User-Agent</code> header is now sent to non-Kimi provid=
ers.</p><p>Also in this release: a provider 413 context overflow now recove=
rs by compacting and retrying first, and compaction output is capped at 128=
k tokens by default to avoid provider <code>max_tokens</code> errors.</p></=
div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span class=3D"wn-=
product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-20-0-june-26-2026" tabindex=3D"-1=
"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.20.0</span> <span class=3D"wn-date">June=
 26, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/co=
de/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-20-0-june-26-2026" aria-label=3D"Per=
malink to =E2=80=9Cv0.20.0 June 26, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h2></div>=
<div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"shell-mode" tabindex=3D"-1">Shell mode =
<a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-c=
ode/whats-new.html#shell-mode" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CShell mo=
de=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>Type <code>!</code> in the input box to e=
nter shell mode and run terminal commands without leaving the conversation =
=E2=80=94 output is written into the context for later turns. For long-runn=
ing commands, press <code>Ctrl+B</code> to move them into the background. F=
or example, run <code>!gh auth login</code> to sign in to the GitHub CLI wi=
thout opening a new terminal. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/cod=
e/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/guides/interaction.html#shell-mode">Shell mode</a><=
/p><h4 id=3D"expose-the-web-server-to-the-internet" tabindex=3D"-1">Expose =
the web server to the internet <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://w=
ww.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#expose-the-web-server-to-=
the-internet" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CExpose the web server to =
the internet=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p><code>kimi web</code> gains a <=
code>--host</code> option to expose the web server beyond your local machin=
e, hardened with token authentication and rate limiting so you can reach th=
e session UI from a remote box. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/c=
ode/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/reference/kimi-command.html#kimi-web">kimi web</a=
></p><h4 id=3D"redesigned-plugin-manager" tabindex=3D"-1">Redesigned plugin=
 manager <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/=
en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#redesigned-plugin-manager" aria-label=3D"Permal=
ink to =E2=80=9CRedesigned plugin manager=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p><c=
ode>/plugins</code> is now a single tabbed panel: <strong>Installed</strong=
> to manage installed plugins, <strong>Official</strong> for the Kimi-maint=
ained marketplace, <strong>Third-party</strong> for marketplace plugins fro=
m other publishers, and <strong>Custom</strong> to install from a GitHub UR=
L, zip, or local path =E2=80=94 switch tabs with <code>Tab</code> / <code>S=
hift-Tab</code>. A confirmation prompt now appears before installing third-=
party plugins. =E2=86=92 <a href=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-=
code-cli/customization/plugins.html#installation-and-management">Plugins</a=
></p><p>Also in this release: fixed a startup crash on Linux caused by a na=
tive clipboard error, and <code>/reload</code> now refreshes plugin Skills =
so plugin changes take effect in the current session without starting a new=
 one.</p></div></div><div class=3D"wn-entry"><div class=3D"wn-meta"><span c=
lass=3D"wn-product">Kimi Code CLI</span><h2 id=3D"v0-19-0-june-22-2026" tab=
index=3D"-1"><span class=3D"ignore-header">v0.19.0</span> <span class=3D"wn=
-date">June 22, 2026</span> <a class=3D"header-anchor" href=3D"https://www.=
kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#v0-19-0-june-22-2026" aria-l=
abel=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9Cv0.19.0 June 22, 2026=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a>=
</h2></div><div class=3D"wn-content"><h4 id=3D"extra-workspace-directories"=
 tabindex=3D"-1">Extra workspace directories <a class=3D"header-anchor" hre=
f=3D"https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/whats-new.html#extra-works=
pace-directories" aria-label=3D"Permalink to =E2=80=9CExtra workspace direc=
tories=E2=80=9D">=E2=80=8B</a></h4><p>You can now add directories beyond yo=
ur working directory to a session: use <code>/add-dir &lt;path&gt;</code> t=
o add one to the current session, or <code>kimi --add-dir &lt;path&gt;</cod=
e> at startup. When you choose to remember a directory, the path is written=
